==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|ang}} {{term|redic}}, {{term|rædic}}, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|radice|rādīce|lang=la}}, the ablative singular of {{term|radix|rādix|root|lang=la}}; later readopted from {{etyl|fr}} {{term|radis}}, from {{etyl|pt}} {{term|raditz}}, from Latin.
[[Image:DSC01796.JPG|thumb|right|200px|a bowl of radishes]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈɹadɪʃ/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈɹædɪʃ/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|es}}

# A [[plant]] of the ''[[Brassicaceae]]'' family, ''[[Raphanus sativus]]'', having an [[edible]] [[root]]
# The [[pungent]] root of this plant, usually eaten [[raw]] in [[salad]]s etc

